# Architecture

Full detail: `docs/02-architecture.md`.

## Monorepo

- Apps are thin: routing, layouts, composition. Cross-route or cross-app code lives in `libs/`.
- `apps/adm` and `apps/bus`: status undecided (`docs/09-known-issues.md`). Do not add code there and do not
  import from them until the decision is recorded.
- Respect `@nx/enforce-module-boundaries` and project tags. Cross-project imports use the path alias, never a
  deep relative path.
- Import direction: `ui` → nothing domain-specific; `feature` → `ui`, `data-access`, `util`;
  `data-access` → `util`; nothing imports from an app. Server-only code is marked `server-only`.

## Route colocation

Every route that owns data or interaction uses this layout. `page.tsx` stays thin. No empty folders.

```text
app/<route>/
  page.tsx      # params, guard, compose sections — no logic
  sections/     # UI composition for this route
  api/          # functions the screen and hooks call — the only data entry point
  hooks/        # server-state and other hooks for this route
  utils/        # pure helpers for this route
  types/        # types for this route
  mock/         # MOCK ONLY — fake data + fake implementations, same shape as api/
```

- `api/` is the only module sections and hooks import for data. In the mock phase `api/` validates input and
  delegates to `mock/` (fake delay + in-memory data). When the real endpoint exists, only `api/` changes.
- `mock/` has `README.md` and a `// MOCK ONLY` header. Never import `mock/` from sections or hooks.
- Existing hybrid mocks (e.g. notification `settings-mock.ts`) follow the same rule and are listed as MOCKED
  in `docs/07-integrations.md`.
- One route uses it → it stays in that route. Two or more routes → `libs/`. The shared UI library never imports
  from a route folder.

## SRS service modules

All SRS services (SRV, Rwd, Dsc, Rfl, Msg, Nws, Nwl, Cln) use the same shape so the pattern repeats:

- Routes per actor surface: public site, user panel (پنل عملیاتی کاربر), provider panel (پنل عملیاتی سرویس‌دهنده),
  admin panel (پنل راهبری). Exact route groups: `docs/04-routing.md`.
- One `data-access` lib and one `types` module per service, shared by all its routes.
- Cross-service behaviours (approval, soft delete, archive, categories, reasons, reports) come from shared libs —
  see `41-shared-patterns.mdc`. Never re-implement them inside a service.
- Before creating the first module of a new service, confirm names with me and record them in `02-architecture.md`.

## Size

A page or component over ~150–200 lines, or with more than one data fetch plus one non-trivial interaction, is
split per `docs/conventions-large-feature-ui.md`.
